id: pmc-claim-evidence
title: Audit every generated release claim against recorded evidence
description: "Emit deterministic claim-to-resolution, tests and delivery map. Overlap: pm CLI 2026.10.21 has no generated-wording audit; pm-changelog classifier chooses sections and entry lint warns on prose; pm-review validates review evidence; pm-ops validates publication provenance. This feature links generated wording to recorded evidence only. Reconciliation PR 266 items excluded."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:59:12.056Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T10:13:22.729Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: A factual closure without repair evidence cannot justify Fixed; absent evidence remains an explicit gap; ordering and regeneration are deterministic.; Typed SDK and CLI; compact TOON/JSON; typed refusals with remedies; README and example; no-git regression; read-only public tracker validation; npm and Bun CI release gates.
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T22:02:55.265Z",codex-agent,"Design: capture exact rendered claim lines through the shared generator, hash generated markdown, deduplicate item evidence, and retain absent resolution/tests/test-result/delivery as explicit gaps. Linked test declarations never imply success; caller-supplied execution receipts require matching commands and retain references. Factual closures preserve classifier-neutral wording. SDK assertions and CLI check refuse unsupported claims. CI will execute full npm and Bun release gates on both supported Node versions; local work uses targeted tests only."
  "2026-10-21T22:09:22.913Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public-main validation at 56f8536702f6d3266825534d502a3dfc947cfb83: 189 complete tracker rows, 165 generated claims, 165 exact line mappings, 165 explicit unsupported claims (no execution receipts supplied), 146 delivery gaps, 39 linked-test gaps, 3 resolution gaps and 1 repair gap. JSON 138556 bytes; TOON 137535 bytes. Reverse-order regeneration byte-identical; complete copied tracker content hash unchanged. Git absent and ancestor discovery disabled. Details: docs/claim-audit-validation.md. Three independent behavioral reverts fail 1/1 each: omit the execution-result gap, omit rendered claim capture, and restore title-only tie ordering."
  "2026-10-21T22:11:05.222Z",codex-agent,"Local evidence: focused claim suite 11/11 via the linked pm runner and direct coverage run; claim-audit source measures 100% lines/branches/functions. Adjacent closure, entry wording, host flag and shipped-doc regressions passed 185/185 before the final focused additions; final new parser behavior passes 2/2. Typecheck, test compilation, docstrings and temporary external ESLint (no-explicit-any and no-unused-vars on every changed source/test file) pass. No lint dependency or pin changed. Existing unrelated strict-unused test imports were observed; they remain covered by the existing static-analysis backlog. Linked execution reports tracking_disabled by project policy, so retain this explicit result receipt. No SDK bug found. Full npm/Bun gates pending CI; thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T22:12:31.885Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/267 at cffc10267c1cbf39c7291535ea0b40463a980245. Full npm/Bun matrix CI started at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/39684735127. Acceptance behavior is implemented; final CI results and claim release will be recorded before handoff. Public PR text was verified for scope, measurements and privacy."
  "2026-10-21T22:14:05.881Z",codex-agent,"CI 39684735127 caught a renderer ownership expectation omitted from the new audit-command contract: Node 26 passed 792/793 with 100% lines/branches/functions across all 16 measured source files; the old assertion named only generate/export. Updated it to include audit; the exact focused assertion now passes 1/1. No implementation or threshold change. Fresh full npm/Bun CI follows."
  "2026-10-21T22:21:12.709Z",codex-agent,"Verified code/test head 1164a41c8f7fec016e71ba1292d55120a6b8d043: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/39685178504 passed both matrix jobs. Node 22 and 26 each passed npm run release:check and bun run release:check: 793/793 tests per gate, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos; 3172 passing executions total. Each gate measured 100% lines/branches/functions across 15 configured source files (correcting the earlier 16-file count). Docstrings: 18 files, 179 declarations. Audit, pack, changelog links/date and publish attestation all passed. Statement coverage remains separately unmeasured. Three behavioral reverts fail 1/1 each. External receipts remain caller assertions; automated reviewer availability is incomplete, not approval. No new PM CLI/SDK defect found. Releasing the claim with the item in progress for orchestrator verification; no merge or release. The next commit contains only this receipt and claim metadata, and its CI will be verified separately."
  "2026-10-22T10:04:10.281Z",codex-agent,"PR 267 review round: pulled remote head, found branch behind main by one commit and merged origin/main before changes. npm ci passed. Read both unresolved threads with every comment and latest CodeRabbit review; no outside-diff section. Both findings valid: conventional Bug Fixes heading bypasses repair gap, and audit command inherits generation intent. Self-review extends semantic category checking to custom grouping and breaking-change copies. Add category metadata at the rendered claim boundary, audit that category, expose audit-specific intent, and independently revert each changed function for regression proof. Keep thresholds unchanged; full npm/Bun gates run in CI."
  "2026-10-22T10:06:21.662Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioral revert proofs: reverting only auditChangelogClaims to its prior section-string check makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"repair assertions\" test/claim-audit.test.ts fail on missing repair gap under Bug Fixes (exit 1). Reverting only the generator emitClaim callback makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"claim source categories\" test/claim-audit.test.ts fail: undefined category instead of Security (exit 1). Reverting only extension activate metadata makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"audit command publishes\" test/extension.test.ts fail: generation intent instead of evidence-audit intent (exit 1). Each variant retained the other fixes; source restored in finally before rebuilding dist. Self-review also covers repair gaps under type/label/status grouping and repeated Breaking Changes entries, plus custom heading Fixed whose semantic category is Security (no false repair gap)."
  "2026-10-22T10:07:58.483Z",codex-agent,"Restored direct claim-audit suite passed 12/12 and audit intent regression passed 1/1, all zero failures/skips; three new regressions passed 3/3 separately. Direct Bun runtime loaded the compiled SDK against a real SDK-initialized non-git tracker and ran the compiled standalone audit CLI with git absent; both checks passed 2/2 and reports matched, including the Bug Fixes repair gap. npm ci, build, build:test, docstrings (18 files/179 declarations) and whitespace checks pass. Full PR diff reviewed for heading-based semantics and copied command metadata; no other unhandled instances. Health retains only existing host extension skew and exact legacy provenance baseline, no pending merge receipts. Full unchanged npm/Bun CI gates required before next PR."
  "2026-10-22T10:13:10.457Z",codex-agent,"Verified source head a4153920a14b16cb4dc0f053363643fe259f51b4 passed CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/39760884830. Node 22 and 26 each passed npm run release:check and bun run release:check, 795/795 tests per gate, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos; 3180 passing executions total. Coverage unchanged at 100% lines/branches/functions across 15 measured source files; docstrings 18 files/179 declarations. Tracker health, production audit, pack, changelog/link/date and attestation checks passed. pm-linked tests also passed 12/12 and 1/1. Three independently failing behavioral reverts and direct Bun real-tracker acceptance 2/2 recorded above. All two review threads fixed plus custom-group and repeated-entry cases found in self-review. No new PM CLI/SDK bug found. Existing statement metric remains unmeasured; receipts are caller assertions. The local clean-HOME gate is still running separately and is not counted as passing. Release claim for orchestrator verification, leaving the item in progress."
